      "kind": "measurement",
      "request": {
        "description": "Characterize compiled dynamics and reset-launch response with isolated saturated actuator pulses across a deterministic official target panel.",
        "measurements": [
          {
            "args": [
              "campaigns/evaluations/e0acf639-be47-4a77-bbc5-fa33eb706033/dynamics_probe.json",
              "--episodes",
              "16",
              "--seed",
              "0",
              "--recovery-frames",
              "20"
            ],
            "artifact": "campaigns/evaluations/e0acf639-be47-4a77-bbc5-fa33eb706033/dynamics_probe.json",
            "instrument": "python_module",
            "label": "compiled dynamics and reset pulse characterization",
            "module": "robot_learning.lab.measure_dynamics"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The initial physical model identifies a consequential distinction between kinematic reachability and dynamic authority from the fully extended reset, with stabilization and target geometry as competing explanations. This candidate-independent protocol measures compiled masses/inertias and actuator transmission, then records every 2 ms state during saturated shoulder/elbow pulses and recovery under the exact scenario reset. Results can determine whether training should first address launch/control authority or whether the dominant next uncertainty is policy-dependent reach, hold stabilization, or inner-radius generalization."
      },
